Found live on amdlab, 2026-10-31 (k290). The cluster's ocpnodes.ocp.internal CRD came from an older OCP and had no spec.nodeIP; `ocp apply --dry-run` and the real run's drift check both said "No drift detected". Only the later "Checking node CRs" step re-applied it, silently. Meanwhile `ocp node add --node_ip` against that CRD lost the field (k290).

Done = OCP::Drift (or the apply pre-check) compares the live CRD schemas of OCP's own CRDs with share/robocop/crds/*.yaml (at least: which spec/status properties the image knows that the cluster does not) and reports a difference as drift with remedy `ocp apply`; `ocp status` shows it; a newer live schema than the image (downgrade) is reported, not "fixed"; tests for both directions.

From k290 (2026-10-31), two small items for the same lane: (1) OCP::Cmd::Apply::CR::ensure_crds returns silently when the CRD directory (share/robocop/crds) is missing, so a packaging error would install no CRD and say nothing. It should die with the path. (2) The OCP::Node POD for spec.nodeIP/status.nodeIP could add one sentence: an OCPNode CRD from before k254 drops both fields without an error, and OCP::Node only ever sees the stored CR (`ocp node add --node_ip` refuses that case since k290).

